<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονοέομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
			<i>have lost all sense,</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of fear, <i>to be
				desperate,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονοηθέντας διαμάχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					6.4.23
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς γνώμαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					16.31.1
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωποι ἀπονενοημένοι</span>
			<i>desperate</i> men, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.81
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				7.5.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of shame or
			duty, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπονενοημένος</span>”
				<i>abandoned fellow,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					6.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				8.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.69
			</span></i>:—later in 
				Act.
			, <i>make desperate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				18.1.6
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
